1
00:00:00,780 --> 00:00:06,210
My name's Liz Fuller and I'm a running coach with Compton Park Runners Club.
我是莉兹·富勒，是康普顿公园跑步俱乐部的跑步教练。

2
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:08,410
Welcome to my podcast.
欢迎来到我的播客。

3
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:12,110
If you're thinking about taking up running, I'm here to help.
如果你正在考虑开始跑步，那么我可以帮助你。

4
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:19,950
There are many training programmes available online which aim to help people build up to running 5 kilometres.
网上有许多训练计划，目标是帮助人们逐渐进步，最后能跑5公里。

5
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:29,800
Some of them are great and thousands of people of all ages are taking part in 5-kilometre races across the country as a result.
其中一些计划很棒，全国各地成千上万的不同年龄段的人最后都在跑5公里。

6
00:00:29,810 --> 00:00:35,170
People like them because they're easy to follow and don't push them too hard.
人们喜欢这种计划，因为很容易跟着跑下来，而且不会给他们太大压力。

7
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:47,430
However, they don't work for everyone, especially if you suffer from something like a heart condition or asthma, because they're aimed at people with average fitness and running ability.
然而，这种计划并不适合所有人，尤其是如果你有心脏病、哮喘等疾病，因为这种计划的目标人群是具有平均健康水平和跑步能力的人。

8
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:57,710
Another thing is that everyone is different, and if you have any specific questions related to your needs, there's no one to provide any answers.
另一个原因是每个人都是不同的，如果你有与你的需求相关的具体问题，没有人能给你提供任何答案。

9
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:03,220
I have a couple of simple tips I always give to new runners.
我总是会给新入门的跑步者提供几个小建议。

10
00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:12,740
I expect you've been told to run very slowly until your fitness increases -- well, I find that can prevent progress.
我想你应该听说过，在你的体力有所改善之前要跑得非常慢，嗯，我发现这样做会阻碍你进步。

11
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:20,940
You should run at a speed that feels comfortable, but time yourself and try to run a bit faster each time.
你应该以一种感觉舒服的速度跑，但要给自己计时，并尝试每次都跑得更快一点。

12
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:28,880
Listening to music can be very helpful -- it takes your mind off things and helps your body get into a rhythm.
听音乐可能会很有帮助，能让你的思绪从其他事情上转移，帮助你的身体进入一种节奏。

13
00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:38,500
I'd say that is better than running with a friend -- especially as most people are competitive and that's not what you want when you're just starting.
我想说，听音乐比和朋友一起跑步效果更好，尤其是因为大多数人都有竞争意识，而刚开始跑步的时候最好不要竞争。

14
00:01:38,510 --> 00:01:47,150
I don't think the time of day is especially important -- some people are better in the evening, while others are morning people --
我认为跑步的时间并不是特别重要，有些人晚上状态更好，有些人早上状态更好，

15
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:57,080
but you need to be consistent, so aim to train regularly -- twice a week is enough to begin with.
但需要时间保持一致，所以争取做到定期训练，开始时每周跑两次就够了。

